{
 "_about": "What canon 0.36.0 accepted for the values `canon-0-37-option-values` narrows (`atip.optionvalues.14`): per option and value class, the commands that took a value of that class. Measured on the released 0.36.0 binary, one run per command on a fresh fixture (the rest by reading the 0.36.0 source: `strategy rollback --reason`, `strategy approval-payload --approver`, and the form-feed and vertical-tab values of the sentence options, which the handlers and patterns of 0.36.0 did not look at). `atip.optionvalues.14` holds the CHANGELOG to this file: every value of it that the build refuses now has a row. Round 2 added the class `other-control` (the control characters of no class of their own): a real-binary probe of 0.36.0 (the reviewer's old-vs-new matrix and a spot check of `finding add --summary` and `scenario new --actor` with U+007F, U+009F, U+0001 and U+001F) shows every cell that took an escape took them too, so each `escape-inside` entry has an `other-control` entry with the same commands.",
 "classes": {
  "empty": "an empty value",
  "blank": "only white space (spaces, a tab)",
  "lf-cr": "a line feed or a carriage return inside the value",
  "tab-inside": "a tab inside the value",
  "escape-inside": "an escape character inside the value",
  "vt-ff-inside": "a vertical tab or a form feed inside the value",
  "nel-ls-ps-inside": "U+0085, U+2028 or U+2029 inside the value",
  "uppercase": "an uppercase letter",
  "underscore": "an underscore",
  "hyphen-end": "a hyphen at the end (`a-`)",
  "hyphen-start": "a hyphen at the start",
  "hyphen-twice": "two hyphens in a row",
  "space-inside": "a space inside",
  "space-around": "a space around",
  "zero": "0",
  "open": "the value `open`",
  "other-control": "a control character that has no class of its own inside the value: U+0001-0008, U+000E-001A, U+001C-001F, U+007F, U+0080-009F except U+0085 (U+0000 cannot be given on a command line); `value` is one of them and `members` the others"
 },
